European Industrial Gases Association. *Cryogenic Vaporisation Systems — Prevention of Brittle Fracture of Equipment and Piping*, Doc 133/22, revision of 133/14. [Complete 33-page publication](https://www.eiga.eu/uploads/documents/DOC133.pdf).

Study the full document, particularly §§4–6 on vaporisers, low-temperature causes and design philosophy, then the protection arrangements and continuing service. It connects available heat, changing demand, downstream material limits and utility failure.

Identity, contents, definitions and selected vaporiser/thermal-ballast passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. Reproduction is permitted with acknowledgement of EIGA. This reading is edition-specific technical guidance; it does not establish a current installation approval. All diagrams and the publication stay external.

